        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(auto-reply): keep export tree truncation UTF-16 safe",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe exported session HTML tree preview must truncate long node text without breaking emoji or other supplementary-plane characters, and it must not scan or allocate the entire message just to keep the first 100 preview characters. Raw UTF-16 slicing could split a surrogate pair, while a full `Array.from(s)` conversion would traverse and allocate for arbitrarily large message text.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe implementation uses a bounded `for...of` scan that stops at the preview budget and slices at the resulting UTF-16 offset. This preserves complete Unicode code points, retains the existing `...` suffix, and avoids full-string materialization. The branch is updated through current `main`, including #107398's independent optional `scrollIntoView` guards and removal of the Linkedom scroll shim.\n\n## User Impact\n\n`/export-session` HTML tree previews keep emoji boundaries intact and remain responsive when a session contains very large message text. The separate #107398 portability fix remains intact.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Exact tested head: `d1adeba8bcbdc0321820bcc3e279b16c391fab2d`.\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/auto-reply/reply/export-html/template.security.test.ts`: pass (`17 passed`).\n- `git diff --check origin/main...HEAD`: pass.\n- `.\\\\node_modules\\\\.bin\\\\oxlint.cmd src/auto-reply/reply/export-html/template.js src/auto-reply/reply/export-html/template.security.test.ts`: pass.\n- oxfmt reports these vendored export-html files are excluded by repository ignore rules; this is not a formatting failure.\n- Exact-head Chrome proof: generated a self-contained export with tree text shaped as `99 x chars + U+1F600 + 500000 y chars`, opened it in headless system Chrome through Playwright, and read `.tree-content` from the rendered page:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"headSha\": \"d1adeba8bcbdc0321820bcc3e279b16c391fab2d\",\n  \"text\": \"user: xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx😀...\",\n  \"emojiHex\": \"1f600\",\n  \"containsEmoji\": true,\n  \"containsEllipsisSuffix\": true,\n  \"containsLongTail\": false,\n  \"loneSurrogate\": false\n}\n```\n\n- Browser proof artifacts were generated locally and were not committed to the repository.\n- Fresh branch-diff autoreview against `origin/main`: pass.\n  - Model: `gpt-5.5` with high reasoning.\n  - Result: `patch is correct` (`0.86` confidence).\n  - Findings: none.\n  - Gate: `autoreview clean: no accepted/actionable findings reported`.\n",
